 "summary": {
  "version": 2,
  "basis": "em",
  "attribution": "Written by a model from the explanatory memorandum; not the record",
  "describes_version": "original",
  "as_of": "2024-05-14",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would appropriate money from the Consolidated Revenue Fund for the 2024-25 spending of the parliamentary departments, as one of three Budget bills alongside Appropriation Bills (No. 1) and (No. 2) 2024-2025.",
   "It would fund the departmental, administered, administered assets and liabilities, and equity injection amounts listed in Schedule 1, with the Portfolio Budget Statements declared relevant documents for interpreting those amounts.",
   "The bill would commence on the later of 1 July 2024 or Royal Assent, and the Act would be repealed at the start of 1 July 2027, in line with the three-year life of annual appropriation Acts."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "A responsible Presiding Officer could add money to an item for urgent, unforeseen expenditure, capped at $300,000 each for the Senate, the House of Representatives and the Parliamentary Budget Office and $1 million for the Department of Parliamentary Services.",
   "Notional transactions between non-corporate Commonwealth entities would be treated as real payments that debit an appropriation.",
   "Amounts could be debited from an item and credited to a special account that shares the item's purpose.",
   "Appropriations could be adjusted under sections 74 to 75 of the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013, including for recoverable goods and services tax and transfers of functions.",
   "Determinations allocating an advance would be legislative instruments that must be tabled but would not be subject to disallowance or sunsetting."
  ],
  "affected": "The Department of the Senate, the Department of the House of Representatives, the Department of Parliamentary Services, the Parliamentary Budget Office and their Presiding Officers are affected.",
